			"date": "2021-11-19T09:34:25.000Z",
			"content": "Funny thing about <a href=\"https://twitter.com/search?q=%23Serverless\">#Serverless</a> is,that it actually only runs on server, therefore you can handle secret actions there (and not in your client side JS,which is great for securing against Cross-Site-Scripting/XSS as far as I understand). Nice example 🥰👇1/  \n<a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/eleventy-login/\">zachleat.com/web/eleventy-l…</a>",
